ition: are they dead code or transitively tested?\n4. Context receipt recovery guard — MODERATE: recovery path silent failure. Countercondition: is the guard redundant?\n5. Torn-tail repair gate — LOW: partial coverage exists. Countercondition: does test_torn_append.py already cover it?\n6. Census delta (11 vs 14) — LOW: observability discrepancy. Countercondition: is it by design?\n\nEach priority has a falsifiable countercondition that would drop it. This makes the ordering criticizable, not dogmatic.","handle":"SCR_002","why_keep_this":"The countercondition gates make the ordering a set of testable hypotheses rather than assertions, aligning with the Popperian framework."},{"content":"Regression test ordering by blast radius:\n\n1. _reset() guard (digest corruption) — append-only record integrity\n2. Lease-mismatch refusal (firewall bypass) — security policy silent failure\n3. Unimported functions (resolve_conjecture_route, compile_criticism_assignments) — routing rot\n4. Context receipt recovery guard — recovery path failure\n5. Torn-tail repair gate — partial coverage exists, marginal gap\n6. Census delta (11 vs 14) — observability discrepancy, unexplained\n\nKey principle: what corrupts the append-only record outranks what hides a refusal, which outranks what hides a routing failure, which outranks what hides a recovery failure, which outranks partial coverage gaps, which outranks unexplained observations.","handle":"SCR_003","why_keep_this":"This ordering encodes the blast-radius reasoning so a maintainer can implement test 1 tomorrow and understand why it is test 1."},{"content":"Are the three pre-v6 roots surfacing as verdicts rather than errors a documented behavior of verify_root_report, or an undiscovered bug? The PARKED.md says 'unexplained, measured only' — this determines whether Priority 6 is a test or a documentation task.","handle":"SCR_004","unfinished":"Unresolved question","why_keep_this":"Related advisory scratch: SCR_002, NEW_001"},{"content":